{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082607-understanding-sympathy","id":1082607,"title":"Understanding Sympathy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-23T07:42:34-07:00","id":1082607,"title":"Understanding Sympathy","content":"It is my understanding that in order to cast a sympathetic spell you need the following<br /> - Space 2's Sympathetic Range Attainment or Time 2's Temporal Sympathy Attainment (only for specific spells)<br /> - Spend +1 Reach for Perception range<br /> - You target something with a sympathetic link to the intended subject, essentially bouncing the spell to them. In the case of Temporal Sympathy you have to target the subject themselves.<br /> - In addition to the above, you need a sympathetic Yanta. It grants +0 instead of its normal bonuses.<br /> <br /> So, here are the the sticking points.<br /> - If you are attempting to Sympathetically cast a spell with Temporal Sympathy, do you need two seperate Yantras? I lean yes.<br /> - Since sympathetic yantras don't offer a bonus, RAW it looks like you can just draw a characiture of the person and use that as a yantra for everything. That reads right, but at the same time feels like it takes the challenge out of finding a good sympathetic yantra?<br /> - Can you use anything with a sympathetic connection as a sympathetuc yantra?<br /> - Can you use the thing with a sympathetic connection as a sympathetic yantra, or do they need to be seperate things?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T08:06:33-07:00","id":1082617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082607-understanding-sympathy#post1082607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You target something with a sympathetic link to the intended subject, essentially bouncing the spell to them. In the case of Temporal Sympathy you have to target the subject themselves</div> </div> </div> </div>To target someone/thing sympathetically you use your own sympathetic connection to the target, there is no bouncing.<br /> <br /> Sticking point 1: The answer is no, you only need one Sympathetic Yantra.<br /> Sticking point 2: Yes, you can just draw a caricature of the person, it's a symbolic yantra. The real challenge of a symbolic yantra is that it's very unlikely to carry any Sympathy to the target that the Mage can borrow in order to establish a Sympathetic connection to the target that can then be exploited for use in Sympathetic casting. In other words it fulfills only one prerequisite for casting a Sympathetic spell instead helping a Mage to fulfill all prerequisites like a Material yantra would.<br /> Sticking point 3: Yes, but only to things that it's sympathetically connected or that it symbolically represents.<br /> Sticking point 4: Don't understand the question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 04-23-2017, 11:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T08:36:15-07:00","id":1082629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082607-understanding-sympathy#post1082607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- You target something with a sympathetic link to the intended subject, essentially bouncing the spell to them. In the case of Temporal Sympathy you have to target the subject themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>With Sympathetic Range you need to personally have sympathy to the target, and using that sympathy you can cast directly on the target. However, it's a 2 dot spell to borrow sympathetic connections from other people and objects so it's not a big deal, but it does mean that they in turn (or their Space friend who borrows the same connection) have sympathy to you personally and can target you with sympathetic spells.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082607-understanding-sympathy#post1082607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Can you use anything with a sympathetic connection as a sympathetuc yantra?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. It needs to fulfil the conditions of sympathetic yantras, meaning that the yantra needs to be a representation of the subject. Body parts, pictures, drawings can be used as yantras. Belongings, friends and family members can not (though they are a great source for borrowing the sympathy).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T09:09:32-07:00","id":1082646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082607-understanding-sympathy#post1082607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, here are the the sticking points.<br /> - If you are attempting to Sympathetically cast a spell with Temporal Sympathy, do you need two seperate Yantras? I lean yes.<br /> - Since sympathetic yantras don't offer a bonus, RAW it looks like you can just draw a characiture of the person and use that as a yantra for everything. That reads right, but at the same time feels like it takes the challenge out of finding a good sympathetic yantra?<br /> - Can you use anything with a sympathetic connection as a sympathetuc yantra?<br /> - Can you use the thing with a sympathetic connection as a sympathetic yantra, or do they need to be seperate things?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. If you are attempting to cast at sympathetic range, while casting temporally, you have to pay both costs according to Temporal Sympathy. I qualify the Yantras as part of the cost, so yes - you need a sympathetic yantra in order to cast sympathetically, and a sympathetic yantra in order to cast temporally. See answer 4.<br /> <br /> 2. Yes, however - if the mage themself has little to no sympathy to the target themselves, that yantra is also likely to be what you are using in order to target them. A lock of hair has a strong connection to it's owner sympathetically, while drawing a picture of someone has no sympathy to them whatsoever. You can utilize this in order to focus on the importance of finding good yantras.<br /> <br /> 3. No - Material, Representational, or Symbolic are the limitations of a yantra. Usually a person does not work for a sympathetic yantra for another person (barring legacy members but that's a whole different can of worms) - its usually things that you can, in some way, tie a person and say 'this is them'.<br /> <br /> 4. If you have a piece of material sympathy which represents a target as well as a certain point of time, I might say that the same piece of sympathy would work - you might not need a whole new object. Mechanically, I would say that you still use 2 yantra slots (if you are gnosis 1 or 2, your out of yantra slots to use) but I personally would say there is nothing stopping you from using the same -thing- as the two yantra's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T09:24:09-07:00","id":1082654,"title":"","content":"Ignore my #3 above, others explained it better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T10:03:13-07:00","id":1082681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082607-understanding-sympathy?p=1082629#post1082629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With Sympathetic Range you need to personally have sympathy to the target, and using that sympathy you can cast directly on the target. However, it's a 2 dot spell to borrow sympathetic connections from other people and objects so it's not a big deal, but it does mean that they in turn (or their Space friend who borrows the same connection) have sympathy to you personally and can target you with sympathetic spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if you think sympathetic links are 2 way things, pretty sure they are one way.<br /> <br /> A's sympathy to B is non existent, B's sympathy to A is also non existent. A borrows a strong link to B. A now has a strong link to B, B has a non existent link to A still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T10:08:24-07:00","id":1082687,"title":"","content":"The only mention of sympathy being one-way was an old post made by Dave. There's nothing in the book that implies sympathy is one-way. In fact, while it's never openly stated the text continously implies sympathy is two-way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T10:39:47-07:00","id":1082707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082607-understanding-sympathy?p=1082687#post1082687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only mention of sympathy being one-way was an old post made by Dave. There's nothing in the book that implies sympathy is one-way. In fact, while it's never openly stated the text continously implies sympathy is two-way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its def two way but is it two different links? I think borrowing threads or web weaving to increase them and giving your target free links back to you is dangerous and one could run it that way. Mages would probably check their sympathy alot more and cast spells to lower their sympathy to something after using a strong link.<br /> <br /> The way i imagine it if that A's link to B is strong its like a huge metal chain, but its my link, B cant use it. B's link to A is weak so it looks like a hemp rope, but its his, i cant use his link and he cant use my link. We can both detect each others link though, B might see A's link and think wtf is this?<br /> <br /> Where the hell is the FAQ??? Did anybody even ask about this in it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 04-23-2017, 01:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T11:04:40-07:00","id":1082712,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure that sympathy is a two way street in terms of sympathetic connections. The connection between a person and their hair for instance is strong - no matter which side of the connection that you are looking at. Your magical tool is strong for you - you can connect to it easily, and it can connect to you easily. A relationship is never really 'two different connections' but one thread which can be pulled at from either side.<br /> <br /> That isn't to say that you cannot, however, have a one sided sympathetic attack - either literally or through the use of spying. If you hold little to no sympathy to someone, and use something of theirs as the yantra - such as their hair, or even a soul stone of theirs - then you have effectively created a scenario where you have a sympathetic tie and they do not - at least not to you. A person -can- follow that thread back to their hair or to their soul stone, but not necessarily to -you- in that sense.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T11:09:32-07:00","id":1082713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082607-understanding-sympathy?p=1082712#post1082712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That isn't to say that you cannot, however, have a one sided sympathetic attack - either literally or through the use of spying. If you hold little to no sympathy to someone, and use something of theirs as the yantra - such as their hair, or even a soul stone of theirs - then you have effectively created a scenario where you have a sympathetic tie and they do not - at least not to you. A person -can- follow that thread back to their hair or to their soul stone, but not necessarily to -you- in that sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats not how sympathy works, you need to borrow/replace the sympathy the hair has to the person over your own. You dont use the hairs sympathy link directly..<br /> <br /> It could also be said and im sure there was 1e essays on this that items dont create their own sympathetic link being only items, sure they pick them up from people and have them by being what they are, but if you put two cans of coke together in a room do they form sympathetic links with one another? I dont think so.<br /> They dont share an emotional link, or a physical one (unless made from the same roll of steel maybe?) and dont usually have a mystical one until somebody adds one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 04-23-2017, 02:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T13:04:32-07:00","id":1082746,"title":"","content":"No. But if you put two people in a room together they don't form sympathy either. However, if they work at the same place, if they barely know one another, etc, they do form a weak sympathic connection. From my read, Sympathy isn't -emotion- so much as -significance-. Those cans of coke that sit next to each other have no significance to each other - but if they were made in the same shop, from the same sheets of metal, tied to the same 6 pack? Might be a weak connection there.<br /> <br /> As far as that not being how sympathy works, I disagree. While it is possible to borrow or replace the sympathy one person has, I'm not sure that's strictly necessary. Consider this - in order to cast against a person utilizing a soul stone or their familiar - do you use your own sympathetic connection to the target, or do you use the sympathetic connection to the familiar or soul stone?<br /> <br /> The answer, by the way, is that you use the connected sympathy - not yours. You ignore withstand, and can target the target without issue. This is why someone having your soul stone is a threat. Sure, one might argue that you needed to borrow the sympathetic connection between that soul stone, but given that requires mastery to borrow, that wouldn't make it much of a threat from anyone besides a space master. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T14:36:37-07:00","id":1082771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082607-understanding-sympathy?p=1082746#post1082746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The answer, by the way, is that you use the connected sympathy - not yours. You ignore withstand, and can target the target without issue. This is why someone having your soul stone is a threat. Sure, one might argue that you needed to borrow the sympathetic connection between that soul stone, but given that requires mastery to borrow, that wouldn't make it much of a threat from anyone besides a space master. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>You use the Connected Sympathy of the Soul Stone by using Borrow Threads, which temporarily grants you a Connected level of Sympathy to your target. So for the duration of your use of Sympathetic magic against a target you and the target share Connected Sympathy. Since magic gives no sign of a build-up unless you're watching the Mage with AMS though, you can blindside them with a spell and then immediately dispel Borrow Threads and they have no recourse to come at you directly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T14:39:39-07:00","id":1082772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082607-understanding-sympathy?p=1082746#post1082746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as that not being how sympathy works, I disagree. While it is possible to borrow or replace the sympathy one person has, I'm not sure that's strictly necessary. Consider this - in order to cast against a person utilizing a soul stone or their familiar - do you use your own sympathetic connection to the target, or do you use the sympathetic connection to the familiar or soul stone?</div> </div> </div> </div>The answer is that you copy the sympathy to yourself with the spell Borrow Threads since the Sympathetic Range Attainment only allows you to cast sympathetically on subjects that <i>you</i> have sympathy to.<br /> The reason you'd want a soul stone or a familiar is because strengthening a sympathetic connection (to mitigate some of the Withstand) requires a 3 dot spell, and it can't strengthen the connection to Connected so you'd still have some Withstand left.<br /> <br /> Edit: What Mrmdubois said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T16:48:37-07:00","id":1082827,"title":"","content":"Soul Stones proxy for their creators for the purpose of sympathy because of their connected nature, so... - still not entirely sure that borrowed threads is a requirement - in the same way that I don't think you'd need to borrow threads from a picture of a person to cast a curse on them. Now - I can certainly see the -benefit- of using borrowed threads, especially if you use it as MrmDubois said and then leave the sensory area of the soul stone; but - here's the breakdown of my logic.<br /> <br /> In order to cast sympathetically you need to have a connection to the subject. Now - strictly speaking, it doesn't actually say that it needs to be -your- connection, just that you have to have a connection in order to do it. If you have a soul stone, you have a connection already - its just not yours. You can target that connection, you can copy that connection, and you can make it yours - but the fact is that you have it to the subject.<br /> <br /> It -does- say that the spell is withstood by the fragility of the sympathetic sympathy between the mage and her subject - and I can see one coming to the logic that that means the connection -must- be the mage's own, and not the connection between whatever objects or people that the mage might have in their possession; but if you accept that for sympathetic range you need to also accept that for temporal sympathy - because it says that there too.<br /> <br /> Now - it is under my understanding that you can enter a room, not have been there at the time - or ever, and still manage to cast a spell even if you have no actual connection to that room. This is - from my interpretation - because you have the room their and -it's- connection to that time line is the same as the temporal connection between the mage and the subject.<br /> <br /> Transfer it over to it's spacial counterpart. Yes - you can totally use your own connections and there is a perfect reason to - but is it <b>required</b>? If you have a lock of hair of a person you just met, do you need to cast two spells - one spell being borrowed threads to -be- connected sympathetically, the other being the spell your casting sympathetically - to use the connection to affect someone you just met to spy on them, or can you use the connection it has already - follow it to the end - and let your spell hit the end of the line?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1513,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","user":"Jakondite","date":". 04-23-2017, 07:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T16:55:51-07:00","id":1082828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082607-understanding-sympathy?p=1082827#post1082827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soul Stones proxy for their creators for the purpose of sympathy because of their connected nature, so... - still not entirely sure that borrowed threads is a requirement - in the same way that I don't think you'd need to borrow threads from a picture of a person to cast a curse on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Per the dev's post from last August:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/941643-help-me-understand-some-uses-of-sympatetic-connections?p=942287#post942287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spells are always withstood by <b>your</b> level of sympathy to the subject; how good a representation of the the sympathetic yantra is doesn't do anything, because it doesn't provide its dice bonus when used to activate the Attainment.<br /> <br /> The way you do things like &quot;ahahahaha, I have a drop of your blood, so I can curse you from across the country&quot; is to cast <i>Borrow Threads</i> on the blood first, and then cast your spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T17:03:57-07:00","id":1082834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082607-understanding-sympathy?p=1082828#post1082828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Per the dev's post from last August: \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. Interesting. Leaves me questions on how to deal with temporal sympathy though - unless its assumed that you use a similar, time version of borrow threads, I'm not sure exactly what the mage's temporal sympathy is with objects he hasn't had or places he's not been before.<br /> <br /> *idly writes up houserules then*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T17:15:50-07:00","id":1082841,"title":"","content":"Temporal Sympathy probably suffers from artifacts when copy-pasting the text from Sympathetic Range. Replace &quot;mage and her subject&quot; with &quot;subject and his past&quot;. You can also remove the line about not knowing the subject's sympathetic name increases Withstand by 1 since the actual text for sympathetic names only mentions Sympathetic Range.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T17:19:33-07:00","id":1082846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082607-understanding-sympathy?p=1082834#post1082834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Leaves me questions on how to deal with temporal sympathy though - unless its assumed that you use a similar, time version of borrow threads, I'm not sure exactly what the mage's temporal sympathy is with objects he hasn't had or places he's not been before.</div> </div> </div> </div>You actually don't have to assume that temporal sympathy works the same way as spatial sympathy just because the Attainments use the same phrase, because temporal sympathy is a thing that subjects have with their past selves, not other entities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T00:16:20-07:00","id":1082925,"title":"","content":"Seriously, I wonder if this whole issue (along with one in the Ask a simple questions thread) could have been avoided by not similarly naming what are three similar yet different concepts.<br /> <br /> Spatial sympathy, the one &quot;sympathy&quot; and &quot;sympathetic connections&quot; refer to by default in most context, is the emotional relationship between two subjects.<br /> <br /> Temporal sympathy is the emotional investment a given subject has to its past selves. Call it nostalgia or something.<br /> <br /> Sympathy Yantras are based on how much the object resembles another subject. Call it Iconic Yantras or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T00:45:48-07:00","id":1082932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082607-understanding-sympathy?p=1082925#post1082925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, I wonder if this whole issue (along with one in the Ask a simple questions thread) could have been avoided by not similarly naming what are three similar yet different concepts.<br /> <br /> Spatial sympathy, the one &quot;sympathy&quot; and &quot;sympathetic connections&quot; refer to by default in most context, is the emotional relationship between two subjects.<br /> <br /> Temporal sympathy is the emotional investment a given subject has to its past selves. Call it nostalgia or something.<br /> <br /> Sympathy Yantras are based on how much the object resembles another subject. Call it Iconic Yantras or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that you then run into arbitrarily-applied poetics in the name of avoiding getting things that are all different elements of sympathetic magic confused, and also that the emotional impact of a connection is effective, not causative \u2014 sympathy is physical/mental/emotional similarity/proximity, which is why Sympathy Yantras work as they do.<br /> <br /> You could refer to spatial sympathies as relations and temporal sympathies as correspondences, but the principle they exploit is still magical sympathy in both cases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T00:52:48-07:00","id":1082934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082607-understanding-sympathy?p=1082932#post1082932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that you then run into arbitrarily-applied poetics in the name of avoiding getting things that are all different elements of sympathetic magic confused, and also that the emotional impact of a connection is effective, not causative \u2014 sympathy is physical/mental/emotional similarity/proximity, which is why Sympathy Yantras work as they do.<br /> <br /> You could refer to spatial sympathies as relations and temporal sympathies as correspondences, but the principle they exploit is still magical sympathy in both cases.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but with all this semiotic clutter and confusion, one can't help but doubt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T13:33:07-07:00","id":1083652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082607-understanding-sympathy?p=1082687#post1082687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only mention of sympathy being one-way was an old post made by Dave. There's nothing in the book that implies sympathy is one-way. In fact, while it's never openly stated the text continously implies sympathy is two-way.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> +2 Reach: The mage may suppress all the subject\u2019s sympathetic<br /> links. This effect applies in both directions; not only does the<br /> 176 chapter four: magic<br /> subject lose his links to loved ones, but those people lose their<br /> links to him. The spell is Withstood by the strongest connection<br /> the subject has. </div> </div> </div>What about this from Veil Sympathy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T15:25:08-07:00","id":1083717,"title":"","content":"I've missed that.<br /> But I'm still not sure about the intended way to handle sympathy. It might be an artifact from an earlier version of how sympathy worked during development, or maybe just an ill worded clarification. The Sympathy section on page 172 makes no mention of sympathetic ties being one way. It's worded &quot;between two subjects&quot; instead of &quot;from one subject to another&quot;, and the example of cutting the sympathetic connection between the married couple talks about a chilled relationship instead of one of the husbands' attitude against the other.<br /> <br /> What I'm saying is that I'm not completely sure about how it should be, but based on the book I still lean towards two way connections. But it might also be bias since I definitely prefer that interpretation. I hope it gets clarified in the FAQ. And I wish <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar14_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"14\" data-vbnamecard=\"14\">Dave Brookshaw</a> got paid for writing it. Both because I want it sooner and because Mage really needs it. (In contrast to VtR's FAQ which I see as a nice bonus.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-25-2017, 06:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T13:09:59-07:00","id":1084117,"title":"","content":"Hmm. How would Temporal Sympathy be handled? It marks deviation or change from the time in question (not outright &quot;ticks since X&quot;, but more &quot;Marvin's changed a lot since the Incident&quot;), yes? What happens when you manipulate that factor artificially?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T18:08:57-07:00","id":1084221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082607-understanding-sympathy?p=1084117#post1084117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. How would Temporal Sympathy be handled? It marks deviation or change from the time in question (not outright &quot;ticks since X&quot;, but more &quot;Marvin's changed a lot since the Incident&quot;), yes? What happens when you manipulate that factor artificially?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is covered in the writeup in the Time Arcanum; strengthening someone's temporal sympathy with a part of their past makes echoing that part more important to them, while weakening it contrariwise reduces its influence on the present iteration of that subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T07:44:18-07:00","id":1084478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082607-understanding-sympathy?p=1084221#post1084221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is covered in the writeup in the Time Arcanum; strengthening someone's temporal sympathy with a part of their past makes echoing that part more important to them, while weakening it contrariwise reduces its influence on the present iteration of that subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, a metaphysical parasite that feeds upon Temporal Sympathy would make its victims care little about their personal historical events, making them more mercurial?<br /> <br /> Conversely, another critter that strengthened Temporal Sympathy (making a &quot;nest&quot; in it?), would cause targets to obsess over maintaining things as they were?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-27-2017, 10:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T07:48:33-07:00","id":1084480,"title":"","content":"I really like those concepts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T08:17:41-07:00","id":1084491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082607-understanding-sympathy?p=1084478#post1084478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, a metaphysical parasite that feeds upon Temporal Sympathy would make its victims care little about their personal historical events, making them more mercurial?<br /> <br /> Conversely, another critter that strengthened Temporal Sympathy (making a &amp;quot;nest&amp;quot; in it?), would cause targets to obsess over maintaining things as they were?</div> </div> </div> </div>The effects would be a little more unpredictable than that. For instance the stronger temporal sympathy might lead to the target obsessing over trying to change from how things were because they don't like their past. Or maybe they don't obsess over their past at all, but they slip back into old habits without even realizing it. Stuff like that. Messing with Sympathy is a much less precise way of influencing others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T04:50:26-07:00","id":1088702,"title":"","content":"Bumping this thread because there's no real place to write this.<br /> <br /> I've been rereading some parts of Mage 2e, and found that the Loved Merit works on the assumption that sympathetic connections are one-way. No other place mentions such.<br /> <br /> My guess is that sympathetic connections are usually two-way, since most emotional relationships are so, but there are circumstances that produce one-way connections if one side's emotions are just that intense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T05:09:26-07:00","id":1088707,"title":"","content":"Feelings don't matter as much as interactions when establishing and maintaining sympathetic connections. And it's difficult to have truly one sided interactions.<br /> <br /> Whether or not sympathetic connections are one way or two way has been discussed extensively in this thread. My own interpretation is that sympathy is normally two ways, but an old post by Dave Brookshaw and some artifacts in the text reveals that sympathy was supposed to be one way earlier in development. But I'm biased since I prefer sympathy to work that way, and others believe that sympathy is still intended to be one way (as in people build up two one way connections towards each other, and spells that affect sympathetic connections only affects one of the connections).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 05-06-2017, 08:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T05:45:51-07:00","id":1088713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082607-understanding-sympathy?p=1088707#post1088707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Feelings don't matter as much as interactions when establishing and maintaining sympathetic connections. And it's difficult to have truly one sided interactions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Feelings do matter<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">: Two subjects may become<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"> sympathetically <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Bold\"><b>linked </b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">when they share a strong <b>emotional</b>,<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"> physical, or mystical connection</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T09:06:02-07:00","id":1088770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082607-understanding-sympathy?p=1088702#post1088702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bumping this thread because there's no real place to write this.<br /> <br /> I've been rereading some parts of Mage 2e, and found that the Loved Merit works on the assumption that sympathetic connections are one-way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. &quot;The force of this thing's love for you prevents you from having a Strong sympathetic connection with anything else&quot; doesn't rely on sympathetic connections having the capacity to be one-way.<br /> <br /> It relies on the Merit's conceit of &quot;weird supernatural entanglement can mess with your sympathies&quot; to make the subject of the Merit the only thing you <i>can</i> form a Strong connection with, while everything else you share sympathy with can then only go up to Medium as part of the defensive purpose of the Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T09:36:04-07:00","id":1088779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082607-understanding-sympathy?p=1088770#post1088770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. &quot;The force of this thing's love for you prevents you from having a Strong sympathetic connection with anything else&quot; doesn't rely on sympathetic connections having the capacity to be one-way.<br /> <br /> It relies on the Merit's conceit of &quot;weird supernatural entanglement can mess with your sympathies&quot; to make the subject of the Merit the only thing you <i>can</i> form a Strong connection with, while everything else you share sympathy with can then only go up to Medium as part of the defensive purpose of the Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">So long as the person or thing that loves you continues<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">to exist, nothing and no one else can create a Strong sympathetic<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">tie with you, though you can form Strong sympathy with them</span></span></span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>I think you have misread the merit: The person with the merit can have as many Strong connections as they like, but only one strong connection from their lover can be made back at them.<br /> <br /> I think nothing &amp; no one else having a strong sympathetic tie with you but you having strong sympathy with them means exactly that its one way, how else could you have a strong connection with somebody when they cant have one with you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T18:44:56-07:00","id":1088941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082607-understanding-sympathy?p=1088770#post1088770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. &quot;The force of this thing's love for you prevents you from having a Strong sympathetic connection with anything else&quot; doesn't rely on sympathetic connections having the capacity to be one-way.<br /> <br /> It relies on the Merit's conceit of &quot;weird supernatural entanglement can mess with your sympathies&quot; to make the subject of the Merit the only thing you <i>can</i> form a Strong connection with, while everything else you share sympathy with can then only go up to Medium as part of the defensive purpose of the Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>This may be the first time I disagreed with you on interpretations of the book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Loved (\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Prerequisite: Sleepwalker<br /> Something or someone loves you. It loves you with enough<br /> force and truth that it has changed the way magic flows to and<br /> from you. <b>This Merit does not imply a return of these feelings<br /> or that you even are aware you are so passionately felt for</b>.<br /> Effect: So long as the person or thing that loves you continues<br /> to exist, <b>nothing and no one else can create a Strong sympathetic<br /> tie with you, though you can form Strong sympathy with them</b>.<br /> Additionally, if you are suffering wound penalties to rolls, or<br /> have spent below half your Willpower, the person or thing that<br /> loves you knows about it. </div> </div> </div>Quote from the pdf, bolded parts mine.<br /> <br /> Here's how I read thos parts: Sleepwalker A is being unknowingly Loved by Entity B. B has a Strong connection to A. A can't have a connection to B, because he doesn't even know who or what B is. Meanwhile, A gets to know Person C. C is a dear friend, maybe even a lover, to A. So A forms a Strong connection to C. However C for some reason can't return the feelings, meaning the connection only goes up to Medium, because of A's Merit.<br /> <br /> The former part I'm not sure of (ie. the question of whether you can have an 'empty' sympathy devoid of actual emotional intimacy), but the latter part I'm quite sure of being how the Merit works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T20:29:55-07:00","id":1088982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082607-understanding-sympathy?p=1088941#post1088941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's how I read thos parts: Sleepwalker A is being unknowingly Loved by Entity B. B has a Strong connection to A.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082607-understanding-sympathy?p=1088779#post1088779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think nothing &amp; no one else having a strong sympathetic tie with you but you having strong sympathy with them means exactly that its one way, how else could you have a strong connection with somebody when they cant have one with you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing about the Merit says that the entity in question has a Strong sympathetic connection with you as a result of its love for you; the only thing the Merit says about the entity in relation to sympathetic connections are how it impacts <i>your</i> sympathies.<br /> <br /> Sympathetic connections are specifically <i>connections between things</i> to the point of being treated as discrete objects by Scale for spellcasting purposes. These are the invisible bonds that make mystically-related characters more easily come into proximity to and familiarity with each other, not just arrows on a relationship web.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T00:38:40-07:00","id":1089035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082607-understanding-sympathy?p=1088982#post1088982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nothing about the Merit says that the entity in question has a Strong sympathetic connection with you as a result of its love for you; the only thing the Merit says about the entity in relation to sympathetic connections are how it impacts <i>your</i> sympathies.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't &quot;nothing and no one else&quot; imply that the Loving entity in fact has a Strong connection? And what do you think about the relation between B and C (in my example)? You're good with logic and language, so your input would greatly help.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Sympathetic connections are specifically <i>connections between things</i> to the point of being treated as discrete objects by Scale for spellcasting purposes. These are the invisible bonds that make mystically-related characters more easily come into proximity to and familiarity with each other, not just arrows on a relationship web. </div> </div> </div>My understanding was it's something like Gauntlet strength, and how it can be high from one side but lower from the other as result of +1 Reach on Place of Power, but is usually the same from either side even when manipulated. There's one connection between two subjects, but its strength could vary in certain circumstances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T01:23:11-07:00","id":1089040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082607-understanding-sympathy?p=1089035#post1089035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't &quot;nothing and no one else&quot; imply that the Loving entity in fact has a Strong connection?</div> </div> </div> </div>It implies that the Loving entity is the only thing that <i>can</i> have a Strong connection maintained with it, but that in no way necessitates that a mystical tie of that strength <i>does</i> exist.<br /> <br /> Feelings and awareness are not the sole determiners of sympathy, and if it did work that way then there'd be very little incentive for mages to seek out pieces of their enemies for the sake of sympathetic magic and very little use in trying to track a mage through the sympathies of their victims even without the time limit of borrowed sympathies, or contrariwise there'd be very little reason to not endeavor to care about as little as possible for as much of the time as possible unless you needed to benefit from someone else's sympathetic magic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And what do you think about the relation between B and C (in my example)? You're good with logic and language, so your input would greatly help. </div> </div> </div>I think you're putting stronger emphasis on the causative role of knowledge and emotion in relation to a supernatural quality that is held by knives and hair in addition to people.<br /> <br /> Consider the role of the supernatural in the ChroD setting; it's regularly obscure, either deliberately or due to some quirk of existence, which means most phenomena aren't going to be attracted directly to people in frequent contact with a deep and wide net of human connections. Odds are good that if you're Loved you're at least isolated enough to be open to the possibility of having the entity in question become just about The Most Important Thing in your life in terms of casual consideration and how your circumstances tend to arrange themselves.<br /> <br /> Only being able to maintain a Medium connection with most people doesn't meaningfully impact the emotional content of your social life; Strong connections are the domain of direct biological relatives, bodily samples, and central long-time nonfamilial relationships, and the only stronger form of connection comes with pregnancy or magic. Being Loved only messes with your dating pool or your nights on the town to the extent that having the attention of any known or unknown supernatural force does in this setting.<br /> <br /> B is obsessed with A with or without a sympathetic bond and continues to be a source of A's Merit. A does not know about this and doesn't really see much in the way of inherent drawbacks to the mere fact of the cap, because a Medium bond accommodates the upper limit of metaphysical intimacy for the vast majority of relationships any given person will have with any given other person. If they have children or their parents are still alive then they might have to exert a bit of extra effort to be quite as close with those people as they would without the damper, but they're not prevented from loving their family just because they're Loved by B.<br /> <br /> A and C become dear friends or lovers or whatever other signifier you would opt to describe the example of a Medium connection with, and this only remotely begins to present an obstacle to their becoming closer in that the natural progression of the universe does not grace the relationship with the same frequency of recurrence as it would if they were best friends/lifelong spouses/murderer and murder weapon and A <i>hadn't</i> caught the eyelike appendages of some spooky nonsense from a dark corner of their house's level geometry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My understanding was it's something like Gauntlet strength, and how it can be high from one side but lower from the other as result of +1 Reach on Place of Power, but is usually the same from either side even when manipulated. There's one connection between two subjects, but its strength could vary in certain circumstances. </div> </div> </div>And this is managed at present by things like Keyed application of Veil Sympathy, but the Gauntlet is a barrier to smooth interaction between two worlds that are inherently reflected at a somewhat-distorted remove from each other where a sympathetic connection literally exists solely as a magical quality signifying how &quot;close&quot; two things are.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's half past four and I have an early shift coming up, so that's a bit rushed as explanations go, but hopefully that helps a little bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T07:03:08-07:00","id":1089121,"title":"","content":"Its really simple. Sleepwalker A has the loved merit coming from B. B Loves A and so has a Strong connection with A. A might love B back (B might also have the loved merit) and have a strong connection to B, A might also have a strong connection to C. But C cant have a strong connection to A because of the merit, so only has a medium connection. Nothing else can have a strong connection to A (only B can), A can have a strong connection to as many things as he likes, even to C even thought C can only have a medium connection back. Note B might only have a medium connection to A, but B is still the only person capable of creating a strong connection with A.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 05-07-2017, 10:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T12:54:33-07:00","id":1089324,"title":"","content":"Just a clarification - the merit actually prevents -others- from forming the sympathetic connections - so that means that it's others that have difficulty getting truly sympathetically close to person a, not person a who has difficulty getting close to others. Sorry, was bugging me - okay moving on!<br /> <br /> Okay - so, bare with me. Reading Sympathy, I'm with Satchel on this one. According to Sympathy: &quot;Two subjects may become sympathetically linked when they <b>share</b> a strong emotional, physical, or mystical connection.&quot;<br /> <br /> Emphathis mine. A Sympathetic Link exists because it's between two people and shared by those people. If one person does not know who the other is, there isn't really a link; The Loved Merit is a bit abnormal in the fact that it changes the way that sympathy works <i>for the character that has it</i>. It isn't -normal- for one person to have a different connection between another - one does not tend to have a strong connection with their lifelong partner, and that partner only have a lovers connection. The Loved Merit changes this - so that if you have a Strong Connection to someone, it is changed to a Medium Connection when it concerns them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T18:01:37-07:00","id":1089494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082607-understanding-sympathy?p=1089324#post1089324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a clarification - the merit actually prevents -others- from forming the sympathetic connections - so that means that it's others that have difficulty getting truly sympathetically close to person a, not person a who has difficulty getting close to others. Sorry, was bugging me - okay moving on!</div> </div> </div> </div>Isnt that what i said? A can have as many strong links as they like to others, the only other person allowed to have strong connections to A is B, all others are capped at medium. The fact A can have strong link to C and C cant have a strong link to A proves links are one way, that and the text from veil sympathy (it mentions in both directions and people loosing links to loved ones and them loosing their links back to you) sold it to me.<br /> <br /> You are probably right in that its not normal for people to have different strength connections between them but they are separate connections, one can via magic or merits be higher or lower. A &lt;-none-&gt;B is more like A -None-&gt;B, B -None-&gt;A until a mage comes along and changes it to A -Strong-&gt;B, B -None-&gt;A.<br /> <br /> Personally i think this whole sympathy links echoing into the fallen world is over played out, If im going to nuke somebody via a sympathetic spell and have a strong connection to them, im not about to think im suddenly in love with them or they are my best friend and decide not to nuke them. Maybe if left long enough it might happen..<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T19:16:35-07:00","id":1089529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082607-understanding-sympathy?p=1089494#post1089494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Isnt that what i said?</div> </div> </div> </div>It might have been? Reading the A-B-C spread isn't exactly working for me (it's very confusing TBH), and honestly I was addressing Satchel in that correction - not you. His example works for what he's expressing, I just wanted to express that it's the other way around.<br /> <br /> As far as the Veil Sympathy statement, that is actually a fairly valid point. I'm of the mind it seems to contradict the statement of what Sympathy -is-, however; Which may be intentional, or may not be. Here is an alternative interpretation - say that a sympathetic link is a two-way street; as the statement of sympathy says it is shared between the two, rather than the individuals own sympathy. You veil your sympathy to your wife; no one can look at you and find your wife's sympathetic thread without clashing. However - if they look at your wife and try to find her sympathetic thread then suddenly they see. Why? Because the wife isn't targeted in the casting of that effect. Kind of like tinting a window one-way so people can't see through it.<br /> <br /> Of course - I will freely admit that that isn't an easy reinterpretation to reach; If I wasn't looking at it as a contradiction of the original writeup of what sympathy was supposed to be, I would never reach that interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1513,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","user":"Jakondite","date":". 05-07-2017, 10:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T22:48:10-07:00","id":1089590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082607-understanding-sympathy?p=1089040#post1089040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Feelings and awareness are not the sole determiners of sympathy<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, so that's the perspective on which this thing works.<br /> <br /> And it seems I do put subconsciously put more emphasis on &quot;...the causative role of knowledge and emotion in relation to a supernatural quality that is held by knives and hair in addition to people...&quot; as you said.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's half past four and I have an early shift coming up, so that's a bit rushed as explanations go, but hopefully that helps a little bit. </div> </div> </div>And you did help. Thanks much.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-03T19:26:32-07:00","id":1551451,"title":"","content":"Major necro.<br /> <br /> So it's clear that someone would have sympathy to their wedding ring, but would the wedding ring have sympathy to them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"rea